{"kind":"stack","id":"s-nutrition","title":"Animals and nutrition: what we eat and why","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1f2d3d","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Nutrition"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The food and drink an animal needs to grow, move and stay healthy."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which of these do animals need to stay healthy?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Food that gives them nutrition","why":"Animals need food to get the nutrition their bodies use.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Only sunlight and water","why":"Pupils may think plants and animals need the same things.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Only fresh air","why":"Pupils may forget that animals also need to eat.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"leaf"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Can animals make their own food?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"No, they must eat food","why":"Animals cannot make food; they get nutrition from what they eat.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Yes, from sunlight","why":"Pupils may confuse animals with plants, which use sunlight.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Yes, from soil","why":"Pupils may think soil feeds animals as it feeds plants.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Balanced diet"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-e","content":"Eating the right types and amounts of food so the body gets all the nutrition it needs."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which food gives a human body protein for growth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Chicken or eggs","why":"Meat, fish, eggs and beans give the body protein for growth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Sweets","why":"Sweets give sugar, not the protein the body needs to grow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Crisps","why":"Crisps mostly give fat and salt, not protein for growth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You are a young fox. Winter is coming and food is hard to find. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Hunt for mice and beetles","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Rest in the den and wait","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You find mice and beetles. Your body gets the protein and energy it needs to stay strong."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"You wait too long. Without food your body gets weak and tired."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Why do animals need to eat food every day?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"To get the nutrition they cannot make themselves","why":"Animals cannot make their own food, so they must get nutrition by eating.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"To make their own sunlight","why":"Pupils may confuse animals with plants, which use sunlight to make food.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"To keep their fur warm","why":"Pupils may think food only keeps the body warm, not that it gives nutrition.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which food gives the body energy to move and grow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Bread and pasta","why":"Bread and pasta are rich in carbohydrates, which give the body energy.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Water alone","why":"Water is essential, but it gives no energy or nutrition.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Air","why":"Air gives oxygen for breathing, not food energy.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you know how animals get their nutrition!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Animals must eat the right food to grow and stay healthy."}],"actions":[]}}
